    <section class="section_anchor legislative_context">
      <p class="eyebrow">DLDV PROPOSAL · WITHDRAWN</p>
      <h2>A proposed 2026 AAMVA image-verification expansion did not become the rule.</h2>
      <p>In the January 16, 2026 Illinois Register, the Secretary of State proposed amending 92 Ill. Adm. Code 1030.140 to allow AAMVA to receive images for comparison through the Driver's License Data Verification (DLDV) Service. The proposal described DLDV customers, including the Social Security Administration, submitting credential information for verification against state records.</p>
      <p>The Secretary of State later published a notice withdrawing the proposed amendment. The April 10, 2026 Illinois Register identifies the January proposal and withdraws the proposed change to Section 1030.140. NoRec therefore records DLDV image-comparison access as <strong>proposed and withdrawn</strong>, not as current Illinois policy.</p>
      <p><a class="text_link" href="https://www.ilsos.gov/content/dam/departments/index/register/volume50/register_volume50_3.pdf">January 16 proposal →</a> · <a class="text_link" href="https://www.ilsos.gov/content/dam/departments/index/register/volume50/register_volume50_15.pdf">April 10 withdrawal →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="section_anchor legislative_context">
      <p class="eyebrow">LEGISLATIVE CONTEXT · NOT CURRENT LAW</p>
      <h2>A 2026 proposal would go substantially further</h2>
      <p>House Bill 5521, introduced in the 104th General Assembly, proposes an Illinois Biometric Surveillance Act and would sharply restrict law-enforcement use of biometric identification systems. As of this page's September 18, 2026 review, the General Assembly lists the bill's last action as re-referral to the House Rules Committee on March 27, 2026.<Citation n={6} title="HB5521 — Biometric Surveillance Act" /></p>
      <p><strong>HB5521 is a proposal, not evidence that its proposed restrictions are currently law.</strong></p>
      <p><a class="text_link" href="https://ilga.gov/legislation/BillStatus?DocNum=5521&DocTypeID=HB&GAID=18&LegId=167496&SessionID=114">View HB5521 on ILGA.gov →</a></p>
    </section>

